[SPEAKER_04]: there we go.

132
00:10:59,417 --> 00:11:01,778
[SPEAKER_04]: I'm going to definitely hear from counselors.

133
00:11:01,818 --> 00:11:12,643
[SPEAKER_04]: I just want to emphasize one point you made and one point maybe you didn't make that I think maybe people should know, but this is an outline of goals and strategies to explore.

134
00:11:13,243 --> 00:11:17,565
[SPEAKER_04]: Actually implementing any of the items in here would require further process, many of them requiring

135
00:11:18,185 --> 00:11:21,267
[SPEAKER_04]: this council to review zoning amendments or other or other items.

136
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:33,295
[SPEAKER_04]: So this doesn't make policy choices today that you know, it's not like all 18 of those items just going to affect tomorrow or whenever we pass it, it's just kind of outlining a plan for things for us to continue to look at in the future.

137
00:11:33,315 --> 00:11:35,377
[SPEAKER_04]: And the other thing I just wanted to note

138
00:11:36,268 --> 00:11:37,868
[SPEAKER_04]: that you mentioned, it's part of state law.

139
00:11:38,249 --> 00:11:53,492
[SPEAKER_04]: There are actually some benefits that could occur to the city were we to pass one, especially around, I believe 40 B, you know, the city's currently under the 10% threshold and therefore developers can come in on a 40 B and build developments outside of our zoning code.

140
00:11:53,532 --> 00:12:01,954
[SPEAKER_04]: This is one implementing on housing production plan as a tool that helps us have protections from, you know, of state law around that.

141
00:12:02,114 --> 00:12:04,415
[SPEAKER_04]: So I just wanted to put those two things out there.

142
