151
00:12:39,723 --> 00:12:48,472
[SPEAKER_00]: if it were to be approved would automatically happen, like trigger some change in the city, or all of these require additional steps?

152
00:12:49,574 --> 00:12:53,097
[SPEAKER_02]: I would say that there's nothing in here that approving it triggers change.

153
00:12:53,157 --> 00:12:56,320
[SPEAKER_02]: These are all a menu of things that we might want to do.

154
00:12:56,801 --> 00:13:00,585
[SPEAKER_02]: And some of these are things that we have already been making progress on.

155
00:13:01,593 --> 00:13:05,894
[SPEAKER_02]: One of them is around adopting an affordable housing trust.

156
00:13:06,274 --> 00:13:08,294
[SPEAKER_02]: As you all know, you've had meetings about that.

157
00:13:08,774 --> 00:13:14,215
[SPEAKER_02]: You did not need this to be passed for you to consider that, for you to choose to do that.

158
00:13:15,196 --> 00:13:22,357
[SPEAKER_02]: So there are things, there's another one in here is around working with more mission-based developers.

159
00:13:22,817 --> 00:13:25,677
[SPEAKER_02]: That is something that our staff have actually been doing.

160
00:13:25,717 --> 00:13:28,078
[SPEAKER_02]: We've been meeting with mission-based developers.

161
00:13:28,618 --> 00:13:41,865
[SPEAKER_02]: So there are things in here that one might say we're already doing, we didn't wait for the plan, but this passing this does not trigger anything with regards to policy or regulations of the city.

